PACK|hardware-triage-2026-05-21|Hardware Triage: NVMe, PCIe, NVIDIA, Dashboard|Safe checks from the Dexter/Baxter recovery: NVMe isolation, PCIe/AER errors, NVIDIA DKMS rebuilds, and dashboard verification. Read-only first. Isolate hardware before repairs.|1.0
ITEM|Quick identity, storage, and network snapshot|hostnamectl && echo && uname -r && echo && lsblk -f && echo && ip -br addr|Shows hostname, kernel, filesystems, mountpoints, and network interfaces/IPs.|Great first command before making changes or asking for help.|identity,storage,network,safe
ITEM|Check key mounts from /proc/mounts|while read dev mp fs opts rest; do case "$mp" in "/"|"/boot/efi"|"/fastdata") echo "$dev $mp $fs $opts" ;; esac; done < /proc/mounts|Shows whether key mounts are read/write or read-only, even when normal tools are acting strange.|Safe no-sudo check. If root flips read-only, stop heavy writes.|mounts,storage,safe
ITEM|Watch storage and PCIe errors|sudo dmesg -T | egrep -i 'i/o error|buffer i/o|ext4-fs error|journal has aborted|pcie.*error|aer|acsviol|nvme.*reset|timeout|abort|input/output error|FAT-fs' | tail -120|Filters kernel logs for storage, NVMe, PCIe, and filesystem failure signs.|If these repeat, stop updates/heavy work and isolate hardware.|pcie,nvme,logs,caution
ITEM|Map NVMe drives to physical identity and PCIe tree|lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,SERIAL,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS && echo && lspci -tv && echo && ls -l /dev/disk/by-id/ | egrep -i 'nvme|samsung|kingston'|Maps Linux device names to drive models, serials, and PCIe paths.|Do not rely only on nvme0/nvme1 names; they can change between boots.|nvme,pcie,hardware,safe
ITEM|NVMe health summary|sudo nvme smart-log /dev/nvme0n1|Shows critical warning, spare, percentage used, temperatures, media errors, unsafe shutdowns, and error log count.|Change the device path to the drive being checked. Zero media errors is good, but link errors can still matter.|nvme,smart,health,caution
ITEM|NVMe error log top entries|sudo nvme error-log /dev/nvme0n1 | head -120|Shows recent NVMe controller error log entries.|Invalid Field can be command/tool related; media errors, resets, and timeouts are more concerning.|nvme,logs,caution
ITEM|Check root file readability without sudo|for f in /usr/bin/sudo /usr/bin/su /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libpam.so.0 /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6; do if [[ -r "$f" ]]; then echo "readable: $f"; else echo "BAD: missing-or-unreadable: $f"; fi; done|Detects whether core root filesystem files are readable when sudo/PAM starts failing.|If these become unreadable, stop and power down or boot rescue media.|filesystem,rescue,safe
ITEM|NVIDIA final check|uname -r && nvidia-smi && systemctl is-active nvidia-persistenced && sudo /usr/sbin/dkms status | grep -i nvidia && lsmod | grep -i '^nvidia' | head|Confirms current kernel, NVIDIA driver, persistence daemon, DKMS module, and loaded NVIDIA modules.|Useful after kernel updates or NVIDIA driver failures.|nvidia,gpu,dkms,safe
ITEM|NVIDIA package and module diagnosis|dpkg -l | egrep -i 'nvidia|dkms|linux-headers' || true; echo; lsmod | egrep -i 'nvidia|nouveau' || true; echo; lspci -nnk | sed -n '/VGA compatible controller/,/Kernel modules/p'|Shows NVIDIA packages, DKMS/header state, loaded modules, and PCI driver binding.|If the GPU is visible but nvidia-smi fails, suspect missing headers or unbuilt DKMS module.|nvidia,drivers,diagnostics,safe
ITEM|Install matching headers and rebuild NVIDIA DKMS|sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y linux-headers-$(uname -r) build-essential dkms nvidia-kernel-dkms && sudo /usr/sbin/dkms autoinstall -k "$(uname -r)" && sudo modprobe nvidia && sudo systemctl restart nvidia-persistenced && nvidia-smi|Fixes the common Debian NVIDIA problem where a new kernel boots before the NVIDIA module is built for it.|Use only after confirming kernel/header/DKMS mismatch. Not a first diagnostic command.|nvidia,dkms,repair,caution
ITEM|Dashboard JSON live preview|curl -s http://127.0.0.1/dashboard/dashboard-data.json | python3 -m json.tool | sed -n '1,140p'|Verifies dashboard data directly from localhost, bypassing browser cache.|Good for checking whether the dashboard JSON is stale or live.|dashboard,json,web,safe
ITEM|Dashboard refresh timer status|systemctl --no-pager status bcbc-dashboard-refresh.timer; echo; systemctl --no-pager status bcbc-dashboard-refresh.service|Checks whether the live dashboard refresh timer/service is installed and running.|Timer should refresh dashboard-data.json periodically.|dashboard,systemd,safe
ITEM|Repair EFI FAT after dirty shutdown|findmnt /boot/efi && sudo umount /boot/efi && sudo fsck.fat -a /dev/nvme0n1p1 && sudo mount /boot/efi && findmnt /boot/efi|Repairs EFI FAT warnings after hard shutdown or power loss.|Do not force unmount. Change device path if needed. Requires dosfstools.|efi,fsck,caution
